# ============================================================================
# EVAL SHEET: "Technical elements of the display"
# ============================================================================
# This file does not exercise any particular geometry — it exists purely so
# the evaluator has something non-blank on screen while poking at the window
# itself. With ONLY this file passed as the program's single argument, check:
#   1. A window opens and stays open for the whole run (doesn't auto-close).
#   2. Hide part/all of the window behind another window, minimize it to the
#      dock, then restore/maximize it. The content must stay correct — no
#      corrupted redraw, no crash, no frozen/blank frame.
#   3. Pressing ESC, and separately clicking the window's red close button,
#      must both exit the program cleanly (no hang, no crash, no leaks).
# If the window doesn't survive expose/resize events, or ESC/close doesn't
# exit cleanly, this whole section is worth 0 regardless of the render.

#ambient strength/ratio RGB_col( , , )
A 0.2 255,255,255

#camera pos( , , ) camera_dir( , , ) field_of_view(in deg)
C 0,0,-10 0,0,1 70

#L pos( , , ) brightness_ratio RGB_col( , , )
L -5,5,-5 0.8 255,255,255

#sp sphere_center( , , ) diameter RGB_colour( , , )
# One sphere is enough to prove the renderer is actually redrawing pixels
# on every expose event, rather than the window happening to still hold a
# stale buffer from the first paint.
sp 0,0,0 4 255,0,0
